 not going to get into a technical  explanation of ray tracing but in basic  terms it allows rays of light to  actually be simulated in a digital  environment so adding a light source to  a scene  automatically produces reflections  bounce light and shadows  the upshot is that you can get much more  complex and realistic lighting with much  less work using ray tracing for example  in these shots see how each little light  bulb is creating its own reflection in  the pictures  this kind of reflection can be generated  almost automatically with ray tracing  but it would have been much more  difficult with traditional 3d lighting  another example of the improvement ray  tracing can provide is the movement of  multiple lights and shadows across  surfaces look at how the light and  shadow moves across the characters in  this shot from toy story  versus this shot on the subway from  seoul we can really see the changes that  ray tracing brought to the scene if we  compare  brave the last pixar film made without  ray tracing to monsters university the  first pixar film to use the technology  the lighting in brave looks good but  in monster's view there's a clear shift  in the quality of the light  especially environmental lighting in  this scene from brave the torches on the  wall look like they're producing light  but they don't really look like they're  actually lighting the environment  compare that to this scene from monsters  university where it genuinely feels like  all the little lights in the scene  are lighting the scene beyond the  improving tools and technology there's  also  large teams and an incredible amount of  attention to detail that goes into  producing the lighting on a pixar film  for example on seoul cinematographer  bradford young whose credits include  arrival selma and solo was brought on to  consult for a variety of aspects of  shooting the film  one being how to light the skin tones of  the black characters and like a real  film set lighting has to be considered  throughout the whole process  in the same way a location manager might  choose a location because  of its access to beautiful natural light  to practically motivate light in an  animated scene there has to be  lights or windows built into the digital  set and the people responsible for  camera movement and composition have to  keep lighting in mind and communicate  with the lighting leads  but for pixar all this effort and the  push for better and better lighting  is not just an avenue to make the films  prettier but one to  allow light to actually play an  increasingly important role  in the story for example look at how the  change in the intensity and color of the  light illuminating joe as a cat helps  cue the emotional arc  of this scene in seoul lighting is used  to help create a clear separation  between the grape before  and earth in the grape before the light  is very soft and diffused it doesn't  have a clear  source and it is very cool in color  on earth harder sunlight creates  interesting complex shadows and  sparkling highlights  look for example at the spectral  highlights on the passing l train or the  harsh  shadows underneath the car these are the  kinds of details that you won't see  in the great before here the source of  the light is often clear  sunlight mixes with practical lighting  fixtures in the digital sets to produce  beautiful rich environments but this  separation isn't just something that  helps define the two places for the  audience  it also plays a crucial role in the  storytelling direct practical sunlight  is associated with earth  as 22 steps out into the world for the  first time in joe's body  22 reacts to the bright sunlight it's  something new that 22 hasn't  experienced before while joe who's  experienced this many times doesn't  react  at all as a side note characters  responding like this like when joe the  cat responds to the warmth of this patch  of sunlight  helps sell the illusion of the light  being real and it illustrates how  lighting  and story have to work together early on  in the process  so soul is creating an association  between direct light with a clear source  and earth but then it also uses this  kind of light to cue  someone's spark when joe plays the piano  early in the film he is backlit by  sunlight coming through a window  this is mirrored later when connie plays  trombone and stands up  into a similar backlight the youth  seminar is a world of  concepts and abstractions souls find  their spark in the hall  of everything but while this hall has  pizza you can't really  taste it the hall might have every  earthly object and activity but there is  still something you can't  find in the hall of everything  [Music]  in this moment light is used to help cue  a spark  that kind of light that is not something  we ever see in the youth seminar  reinforcing the idea that  22 spark had to be found on earth  that 22 spark wasn't an abstract concept  but something as tangible as the warmth  and beauty of sunlight  but the spark is not just the object of  the seed or the light streaming through  the trees  it's all of these things it's the  feeling produced by this  mundane beauty the idea that this thing  exists that there is something that is  not found in the hall  of everything but that exists on earth  in this moment  essential to the film's philosophy and  premise  and because this thing isn't a concept  or object it's not something that can be  described in the film  it's a feeling it has to be evoked in  the audience  joe's later realization that 22's spark  was the joy of everyday living while he  looks at this seed would have had less  impact if the way the backlight  illuminates the veins in the seed wasn't  so genuinely  beautiful the beauty of the film's  naturalistic lighting on earth  in contrast to the pretty but more  conceptual abstract feeling of the great  before  helps communicate the film's philosophy  that there's a unique  important quality to life on earth that  lies  outside of abstraction and concepts  that there's a value in everyday living  outside of our list of accomplishments  and that would be a difficult concept to  convey if you couldn't show  that beauty 22 spark is getting to  experience  the beauty of such a simple moment and  for the audience to believe it  and feel it that moment had to actually  be beautiful  one of the most important ingredients in  the beauty of this moment  is the light  [Music]  this video is sponsored by surf shark  vpn use code thomasflay or click the  link in the description to get 83  off and three months for free of your  subscription to  surfsharkvpn vpns are services that  allow you to route all your internet  traffic through servers all around the  world this can have a lot of privacy and  security benefits and allow you to take  back some of the control and privacy of  your internet usage from your isp  you can avoid things like location based  price discrimination or  region locked streaming content if you  live in a country that bands or blocks  certain internet services or websites  vpns are a crucial tool for getting  around censorship  surfsharkvpn is an affordable vpn with a  lot of great features and  a 30-day money-back guarantee one of my  favorite surfshark features is that on  their windows application you can  whitelist  certain applications so one application  can be routing through the vpn while  another is running through your normal  internet click the link in the  description or use the code  thomasflight to get 83 off your  subscription  and three months for free thanks again  to surfshark for supporting this video  and making it possible  [Music]  you

